diffs.notes:
Build: an official Nokia build (MIDlet-Vendor Nokia, Created-By 1.3.1.02 Hewlett-Packard Co., the same toolchain as 1.8). Class and resource files are dated 2 Oct 2002, against 10 Dec 2002 for 1.8. It is unobfuscated, with LineNumberTables, and uses MIDP-1.0/CLDC-1.0 with Nokia FullCanvas, DirectGraphics and Sound. This is the earliest build in the set. 1.8 reads as a bug-fix of it: the closed exit becomes solid, hoop rims are added, the left-edge flip is fixed, a ±150 speed clamp, a wall bounce and halved plain-ramp redirects are added, the ring water flag is kept, the dirty bit is masked in collisions, the floor bounce ends the vertical loop, the roof rebound goes from 6 to 20, and pause-on-hide plus the left soft key are added.

Identical to 1.8: all 11 level files (byte-identical); bouncesplash.png, icon.png and nokiagames.png; Profile.class; the collision masks TRI_TILE_DATA, SMALL_BALL_DATA and LARGE_BALL_DATA; gravity, jump, friction and acceleration constants (-67, -10, -80, 4/6/3/-2, 80/42/38/-30, 50/100, 6, 4); scoring (ring 500, gem 200, life 1000 with max 5 lives, exit 5000) and 3 starting lives; 11 levels; spike movement (updateMovingSpikeObj positions); exit opening (4 px per step to 24); camera code testScroll, scrollBuffer, cleanBuffer and createNewBuffer, plus createBufferFocused apart from the gc; the step order in BounceCanvas.run(); the cheat codes; the RMS layout; screen layout (buffer 156x96, 13x8 tiles of 12 px, HUD band y=97..128 colour 0x0853AA, lives at y=99, rings at y=112, score at (64,100), 'Level N' at (44,84) for 120 steps, bonus bar at x=1); and the splash flow.

For a 1.01 mode in js/rules.js, the 1.01 vertical loop is:

  for (i=0; i < abs(ySpeed)/10; i++) {   // bound re-read every pass
    s = sign(ySpeed);
    if (free(x, y+s)) { y += s; grounded = false; [large-ball water exit: ySpeed /= 2, |ySpeed|<=10 → 0] }
    else {
      ramp slide as in 1.8;
      if (s>0 || rev&&s<0) { ySpeed = -ySpeed/2; grounded = true; rubber/jumpOffset logic as in 1.8; if (|ySpeed|<10) ySpeed = rev ? -10 : 10; /* no break */ }
      else if (s<0 || rev&&s>0) ySpeed = rev ? -6 : 6;
    }
  }

There is no ±150 clamp before it.

1.01 collisionDetection(x, y):
  k = 0; if (y < 0) { k = |y|/12 + 1; y = 0; }
  rows (y-half)/12 - k up to (y-1+half)/12 (inclusive); gy = y - half - 12k + tileY*12.

testTile uses tile & ~0x40, so a tile with the 0x80 bit counts as empty. Passable tiles: 0, 8, 25-28, the closed exit 9, and any tile with 0x80. Hoops have no rims. Collected-hoop tiles get the plain values 145-156 (no water bit).

Paths in the entries are relative to each version's cfr/com/nokia/mid/appl/boun/ (Java) or x/ (resources). Helper scripts (level scanner, OTT decoder, lang decoder) and javap dumps are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/9e293dcf-c6a7-5416-93b2-b9c9546fbcbb/scratchpad/work/versions/v1.01/.
